  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "##  🔍Teacher Notes\r\nThis activity is from <a href='https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-v2-2025/units/1/lessons/3' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>Lesson 3</a>. We've modified this activity for PL in two ways:\r\n1. Combined three separate curriculum levels into one.\r\n2. Turned partner discussion into individual reflections.\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Minimal Context Given\r\n\r\nPractice prompting through the career of a travel agent by giving a simple, unstructured prompt to see how AI makes recommendations without any specific details or examples.\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Try a basic prompt like the one below, or a similar one related to family vacations.\r\n\r\n>Recommend a family vacation destination.\r\n\r\n2. Press **Send**.\r\n3. Read the response you get, paying attention to how useful or generic the recommendation is.\r\n\r\n---\r\n## 2. Providing a Single Example\r\n\r\nPractice prompting through the career of a travel agent by adding a single example to help guide the AI's recommendation.\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Decide on **a brief example of a vacation destination.**\r\n2. Prompt AI to recommend a family destination by including your example.\r\n2. Press **Send**.\r\n3. Read the response you get, paying attention to how the AI builds on your example to make a more specific or relevant suggestion.\r\n\r\n::: details [**Not sure where to start?**]\r\nHere's an example prompt:\r\n> Recommend a vacation destination for a family of four that enjoys outdoor adventures and cultural experiences. For example: \r\n>\r\n> The Bahamas offers beautiful beaches and family-friendly resorts. \r\n:::\r\n\r\n---\r\n## 3. Providing Multiple Examples\r\n\r\nPractice prompting through the career of a travel agent by giving the AI a detailed and structured request that includes multiple expectations.\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Prompt AI to recommend a family destination by including **several examples** of vacation destinations.\r\n2. Before sending it, think about the difference between your prompt on this level and the previous one.\r\n2. Press **Send**.\r\n3. Read the response you get, paying attention to how the added context improves the accuracy, relevance, and usefulness of the recommendation.\r\n\r\n::: details [**Not sure where to start?**]\r\nHere's an example prompt:\r\n> Recommend a vacation destination for a family of four that enjoys outdoor adventures and cultural experiences. For example: \r\n>\r\n> The Bahamas offers beautiful beaches and family-friendly resorts.\r\n>\r\n> OR\r\n> \r\n> Palm Springs offers many nearby hiking opportunities and mini-golf adventures.\r\n>\r\n> OR\r\n> \r\n> Thailand offers jungle excursions and lunar themed parties.\r\n:::",
